0046:     Input structure
0047:     - The input is a black 2-row strip containing 4-connected red glyphs, read left to right.
0048:     - Each glyph spans both rows and has exactly one top red entry cell; its bottom row is either the same cell only or a two-cell elbow.
0049:     Rule
0050:     - Make a black output whose width is one more than half the input width and whose height is one marker row plus one row for each elbow and two rows for each vertical glyph.
0051:     - Put a green marker in the center of the top row, then trace the glyphs downward: a vertical glyph paints two red cells in the current column; an elbow paints the two bottom cells as a horizontal red segment and moves the current column left or right.
0052:     Key insight
0053:     - The missing top cell of each 2x2 elbow tells whether the trace exits left or right; the glyphs are pipe instructions rather than shapes to copy literally.
0054:     """
